Adds a weight-update session API for quantized rollout engines.
begin_weight_update restores in-place-packed weights (e.g. Marlin-repacked)
to a loadable state before new weights arrive; end_weight_update optionally
runs post_load_weights (when load_weights was bypassed, e.g. P2P/RDMA) and
finalizes quantized weights back into kernel layout. Exposed as HTTP
endpoints and wired through tokenizer manager, scheduler, weight updater,
and model runner, with a {target, draft, all} selector so the draft model
is prepared identically to the target. Also implements iter_runners() on
the 5 speculative workers so draft runners are included under speculative
decoding.

